WEBVTT

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:19.750
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:19.750
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:19.750
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:48.050
Wasn't the cause of the defeat of the Imperial
Fleet the acute intoxication of the sailors...

00:01:48.050 --> 00:01:51.900
...the result of the vaporization of the
drug that triggered hallucinations ?

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:52.770
Why ?

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:56.430
Why did you extend yourself that far
to cover for Vice Admiral Basel ?

00:01:59.410 --> 00:02:02.520
It's not really a difficult
question to answer.

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:07.930
The man she chose, whom Johanna
chose, cannot be a criminal.

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:16.960
Johanna chose a man who was worthy of her,
a man of integrity and substance, her equal.

00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:18.610
That's...

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:25.870
But justice or love can sometimes be nothing
but a burden to those who are its recipients.

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:29.700
Life is not elementary arithmetic.

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:32.590
Formulas can't find
solutions for everything.

00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:39.650
If we knew a certain amount of reward would result from a certain amount of devotion...

00:02:39.650 --> 00:02:42.670
...life would be so
simple and clear.

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:50.160
Commander, you are right,
more right than I am.

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:53.090
If I had publicized the
facts three years ago...

00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:58.420
...I could have at least prevented new
Thyoxin addiction cases afterwards.

00:02:59.910 --> 00:03:05.120
I sacrificed those soldiers
for my own sentimentality.

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:10.900
They too must have had people they loved,
things they wanted to pursue or protect.

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:14.960
I was an intractable narcissist.

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:18.020
I brought no one happiness.

00:03:19.610 --> 00:03:22.850
He did not look for compensation
in his devotion toward Mrs. Basel.

00:03:22.850 --> 00:03:25.950
Is it a noble feeling ?

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:29.400
Or is it just egoism ?

00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:39.600
Dishonor

00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:39.600
Chapter 4

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:48.100
How did it go, Commander ?

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:52.480
It didn't work out, did it ?

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:58.950
He told me the truth of the affair,
but said that he cannot testify in court.

00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:07.780
Even if he has no intention of testifying the perpetrator might try to silence him.

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:09.840
Don't let anyone
near this room.

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:11.200
Yes, sir.

00:04:12.990 --> 00:04:14.850
How about the
man we arrested ?

00:04:14.850 --> 00:04:20.420
Just as we thought, he said he was a
mercenary and had no idea who his client was.

00:04:20.420 --> 00:04:21.430
I see.

00:04:22.390 --> 00:04:24.520
Both now and
three years ago...

00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:30.770
...the one in charge of Thyoxin
trafficking is Retired Vice Admiral Basel.

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:34.650
Most likely, Mrs. Basel
is aware of that fact.

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:47.190
Mr. Basel and Mrs. Basel are
staying in separate rooms.

00:04:53.910 --> 00:04:56.320
It seems that because they came
earlier than was scheduled...

00:04:56.320 --> 00:04:59.290
...only separate single
rooms were available.

00:04:59.960 --> 00:05:05.400
The fact that they had to accept such
inconvenience to arrive ahead of schedule...

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:07.900
...is indicative of the
strangeness of their actions.

00:05:20.650 --> 00:05:23.600
I heard you came here
in place of Michael.

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:24.620
Thank you for the trouble.

00:05:25.140 --> 00:05:27.820
Yes, for some reason,
that's how things turned out.

00:05:36.590 --> 00:05:38.240
To tell you the truth...

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:40.840
I gather you'll be asking for my
understanding of the circumstances...

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:49.050
...in which Michael would disclose the crimes
committed by my husband, Christopher.

00:05:49.900 --> 00:05:52.560
Why do you think so ?

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:57.200
Because I was the one who informed the 
police that the head of the drug organization...

00:05:57.200 --> 00:06:00.160
...would be coming
to this satellite.

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:01.490
Just as I thought.

00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:08.650
I also sent an anonymous tip to Christopher that there is someone who knows of his crimes...

00:06:08.650 --> 00:06:12.820
...and that if he quit now, the information
wouldn't be forwarded to the Military Police.

00:06:12.820 --> 00:06:14.910
But it backfired.

00:06:15.950 --> 00:06:21.840
Vice Admiral Basel thought that the
tip was blackmail by Lord Keyserling.

00:06:22.460 --> 00:06:25.850
Therefore he sent an
addict to silence him.

00:06:25.850 --> 00:06:32.000
And to discover the outcome, he had to
come to Kreuznach III ahead of the schedule.

00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:36.450
Yes, young man,
just as you speculate.

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:40.390
It may have been impossible
for you to predict...

00:06:40.390 --> 00:06:44.030
...how your anonymous message
would endanger Lord Keyserling.

00:06:44.030 --> 00:06:50.460
But you probably knew why Vice Admiral Basel
came here ahead of schedule, didn't you ?

00:06:50.460 --> 00:06:54.860
If you'll excuse me, Lord
Keyserling was in love with you.

00:06:54.860 --> 00:07:00.500
At the risk of being intrusive, couldn't
you be a little more considerate of him ?

00:07:06.270 --> 00:07:12.520
Young man, it does not
matter who loves me;

00:07:12.520 --> 00:07:16.050
What matters
is whom I love.

00:07:20.650 --> 00:07:26.800
I knew all along that Michael was a person of
more integrity and goodness than Christopher.

00:07:27.600 --> 00:07:29.650
But, young man...

00:07:29.650 --> 00:07:34.050
...there is no correlation between how highly
you evaluate someone as a human being...

00:07:34.050 --> 00:07:36.050
...and how much you love him.

00:07:38.300 --> 00:07:43.050
About a year ago, I found out that 
my husband was committing crimes...

00:07:43.050 --> 00:07:48.650
...that cannot be forgiven under
any government, in any era...

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:52.050
...and also that he escaped his
punishment three years ago...

00:07:52.050 --> 00:07:55.110
...by taking advantage of
Michael's feelings for me.

00:07:55.110 --> 00:07:56.230
Then...

00:07:56.950 --> 00:07:58.790
I cannot betray my husband.

00:07:59.600 --> 00:08:03.910
But I wanted him to apologize
for his crime to Michael.

00:08:03.910 --> 00:08:06.750
To this end, I proposed that
three of us meet here...

00:08:06.750 --> 00:08:09.840
...the same place we met for
the first time forty years ago.

00:08:10.250 --> 00:08:13.460
And I played the aforementioned
trick on them also.

00:08:13.460 --> 00:08:18.650
But when my husband decided to come
here two days ahead of schedule...

00:08:18.650 --> 00:08:21.150
...my thoughtless
scheme failed.

00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:53.910
At this point, we've
only got one strategy.

00:08:53.910 --> 00:08:59.390
It's risky, but I'll ask for
your cooperation once again.

00:08:59.390 --> 00:09:00.950
What are you planning to do ?

00:09:00.950 --> 00:09:05.200
Well, sometimes, bluffing
can be a necessary evil.{gesture.}

00:09:08.370 --> 00:09:10.700
Well, well, Commander Kircheis.

00:09:10.700 --> 00:09:14.290
It's an honor to have
you visit my room.

00:09:14.600 --> 00:09:15.600
Please come in.

00:09:19.020 --> 00:09:22.830
Surely, he's got a lot of swagger,
to the point of shamelessness.

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:26.710
So what brings you here ?

00:09:27.380 --> 00:09:29.690
I ask you not
to feign ignorance.

00:09:29.690 --> 00:09:33.880
A while ago, I was attacked
in town by five men.

00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:37.230
Four of them died,
but one was arrested.

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:40.460
What trouble for you.

00:09:40.460 --> 00:09:44.490
But how does
that concern me ?

00:09:44.490 --> 00:09:50.650
The arrested man confessed that you,
Retired Vice Admiral Basel, gave the order.

00:09:51.050 --> 00:09:52.220
That's impossible !

00:09:55.370 --> 00:09:57.480
Why is that ?

00:09:57.480 --> 00:10:00.360
You didn't disclose
your identity to them.

00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:03.190
There was no way we
could trace them to you.

00:10:03.190 --> 00:10:05.340
That's what you're thinking, isn't it ?

00:10:06.320 --> 00:10:08.690
Looks like I've fallen
for your cheap trick.

00:10:09.310 --> 00:10:12.150
But they were truly useless.

00:10:12.150 --> 00:10:15.560
Five on one and they
couldn't pull off the job.

00:10:16.530 --> 00:10:19.490
Regrettably, I have to
acknowledge my mistake.

00:10:19.490 --> 00:10:21.210
So now we can talk business:

00:10:21.210 --> 00:10:24.500
How much do you want me to pay
you to keep quiet, Commander ?

00:10:26.150 --> 00:10:30.950
I have no desire to gain from the profit
you made unjustly from the war.

00:10:31.900 --> 00:10:36.650
Oh well, you're a grownup in
height but just a kid in reality.

00:10:36.650 --> 00:10:41.050
Wars exist in the first place because
they are a profitable enterprise.

00:10:41.050 --> 00:10:47.300
Think about it: wars happen because
there are people who benefit from them.

00:10:47.300 --> 00:10:49.650
If no one profited from it...

00:10:49.650 --> 00:10:53.100
...such a useless social system wouldn't
have continued on till this day.

00:10:53.100 --> 00:10:55.950
And so long as it
continues to exist...

00:10:55.950 --> 00:10:59.910
...isn't it wiser to find a way to utilize
it effectively to your advantage ?

00:10:59.910 --> 00:11:03.320
I have no desire to philosophize
about war with you.

00:11:05.550 --> 00:11:10.050
To perceive the reality of war, to
affirm it, or to take ill advantage of it...

00:11:10.050 --> 00:11:11.830
...those are not
the same thing.

00:11:11.830 --> 00:11:15.400
What makes you think you have the
right to make the soldiers suffer...

00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:18.180
...both mentally and physically,
for your own ends ?

00:11:18.790 --> 00:11:24.310
Pigs exist to be eaten by humans;
they don't live to eat humans.

00:11:24.310 --> 00:11:26.400
A magniloquent way of
saying it would be to say...

00:11:26.400 --> 00:11:28.210
...that it's the natural law
of the universe, Commander.

00:11:28.520 --> 00:11:30.300
Are soldiers pigs ?

00:11:30.610 --> 00:11:32.030
Did that make you angry ?

00:11:32.030 --> 00:11:38.800
But even the Prince climbed to his present
glory by making soldiers die in the war, right ?

00:11:38.800 --> 00:11:42.690
The Prince played it within the
accepted norm; I went a little too far.

00:11:42.690 --> 00:11:44.450
That's the only difference.

00:11:44.450 --> 00:11:47.400
No, at least, Lord Reinhard...

00:11:47.400 --> 00:11:48.810
...no, Admiral Musel...

00:11:48.810 --> 00:11:51.210
...has never fought
for private gain !

00:11:52.270 --> 00:11:53.870
What hypocrisy.

00:11:53.870 --> 00:11:55.280
But that's fine.

00:11:55.280 --> 00:11:58.880
Then what do you want
to do, righteous Commander ?

00:11:58.880 --> 00:12:01.110
Are you going to indict me ?

00:12:01.190 --> 00:12:02.330
That's all lovely.

00:12:02.330 --> 00:12:04.950
But you have no evidence
to indict me with.

00:12:05.520 --> 00:12:08.670
Isn't it wiser to
consider my proposition ?

00:12:09.160 --> 00:12:14.350
Instead of physical evidence we have the
testimony from Retired Rear Admiral Keyserling.

00:12:14.350 --> 00:12:16.380
A complaint by
a love-lost man ?

00:12:16.380 --> 00:12:17.430
How silly.

00:12:17.430 --> 00:12:21.100
People will just consider
it his jealousy-driven delusion.

00:12:21.100 --> 00:12:25.010
Then I will have your
wife testify, too.

00:12:25.700 --> 00:12:27.050
Johanna ?

00:12:28.050 --> 00:12:30.010
The lady knows everything, too.

00:12:30.010 --> 00:12:34.060
She's the one who sent
the warning message to you.

00:12:34.780 --> 00:12:37.840
She was hoping that you would take the
warning to heart and regret your actions...

00:12:37.840 --> 00:12:40.900
...that you would apologize to Lord
Keyserling for dishonoring him...

00:12:40.900 --> 00:12:45.190
...and for evading your own
accountability three years ago, but...

00:12:45.190 --> 00:12:48.600
...you dashed her hopes.

00:12:48.910 --> 00:12:55.710
I see, Johanna tried to quell her feelings of
guilt for rejecting Michael by such an action.

00:12:58.400 --> 00:13:02.240
In that scenario, the one who would
apologize is not her, but me.

00:13:02.240 --> 00:13:03.520
How selfish.

00:13:05.050 --> 00:13:07.120
Is that how
you think of it ?

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:09.880
That's why I've been able
to survive to this day !

00:13:24.450 --> 00:13:28.960
Commander Kircheis, you seem to be
a man of honorable character...

00:13:28.960 --> 00:13:32.860
...but unless you learn to be
more clever, you won't live long.

00:13:32.860 --> 00:13:33.830
I don't need your advice !

00:13:34.260 --> 00:13:36.370
"Unnecessary" help, eh ?

00:13:36.370 --> 00:13:42.290
But from my standpoint, what Keyserling
did three years ago was precisely that.

00:13:42.950 --> 00:13:46.400
Even though I never asked for it,
he took my part of the accountability...

00:13:46.400 --> 00:13:48.050
...and force-fed me a
tacit debt of gratitude.

00:13:48.050 --> 00:13:49.800
He's always been...

00:13:51.830 --> 00:13:54.690
Are you done with your
conversation, Commander ?

00:13:54.690 --> 00:13:56.990
Retired Vice Admiral Basel...

00:13:56.990 --> 00:14:00.950
...I arrest you in the act of the
crime of attempted murder.

00:14:00.950 --> 00:14:02.340
That's hogwash !

00:14:02.340 --> 00:14:04.020
Look at the
handgun over there.

00:14:04.020 --> 00:14:05.960
I was the one who
was almost killed.

00:14:06.630 --> 00:14:08.310
This was righteous self-defense.

00:14:15.260 --> 00:14:18.960
I'm sorry to tell you, but we've been
observing what happened inside the room.

00:14:18.960 --> 00:14:20.460
Everything has been recorded.

00:14:21.050 --> 00:14:26.870
Lord Basel, that includes your own statement in which you admitted your part in drug smuggling.

00:14:27.610 --> 00:14:31.190
Such evidence isn't
admissible in court !

00:14:31.190 --> 00:14:35.110
If you find a skilled lawyer,
it might be difficult.

00:14:35.110 --> 00:14:40.760
But it'll probably provide enough grounds to search your belongings in this room for the time being.

00:14:41.370 --> 00:14:43.250
To search my belongings ?

00:14:43.250 --> 00:14:45.400
You're just police, you'd
better know your place !

00:14:45.930 --> 00:14:48.330
I'm a Retired Vice Admiral
of the Imperial Fleet.

00:14:48.330 --> 00:14:51.050
Don't think you can treat me
like just another civilian !

00:14:51.510 --> 00:14:56.880
I'm sorry to tell you, but for felonies
like murder and drug-related crimes...

00:14:56.880 --> 00:14:59.910
...one's social position need
not be a consideration...

00:14:59.910 --> 00:15:05.760
...according to the rules and regulations
of the Ministry of Home Affairs.

00:15:05.760 --> 00:15:07.110
Bureaucratic ass.

00:15:07.110 --> 00:15:12.330
Do you think you can arrest a retired admiral
based on the rules of just one ministry ?

00:15:12.330 --> 00:15:14.620
You make me laugh.

00:15:14.620 --> 00:15:17.910
If you don't like it, you can talk to the Ministry of Military Affairs...

00:15:17.910 --> 00:15:20.510
...and protest to the
Ministry of Home Affairs.

00:15:20.510 --> 00:15:24.050
But if we search your belongings,
firmer evidence will be discovered.

00:15:24.050 --> 00:15:26.150
In that case, the
result will be the same...

00:15:26.150 --> 00:15:31.600
...whether you're tried in a
military or civilian court.

00:15:36.190 --> 00:15:37.440
I see.

00:15:37.440 --> 00:15:39.560
It seems I've lost.

00:15:40.110 --> 00:15:42.130
I'll acknowledge that.

00:15:42.130 --> 00:15:45.120
Lastly, I'd like
to talk to my wife.

00:15:45.120 --> 00:15:46.130
I ask for your permission.

00:15:48.130 --> 00:15:48.820
Please go ahead.

00:15:59.390 --> 00:16:01.760
Johanna, it's me.

00:16:01.760 --> 00:16:06.510
My briefcase is on the desk
in your room, isn't it ?

00:16:06.510 --> 00:16:08.400
Burn the contents
of that briefcase !

00:16:09.600 --> 00:16:11.400
You heard me.

00:16:11.400 --> 00:16:13.500
I only said "contents."

00:16:13.500 --> 00:16:15.950
How are you going to prove that
it's the evidence of my crime ?

00:16:16.580 --> 00:16:18.180
Why you...

00:16:19.440 --> 00:16:20.210
Arrest him !

00:16:20.580 --> 00:16:21.330
Yes, sir !

00:16:30.880 --> 00:16:33.250
Frau Basel, please open the door.

00:16:46.950 --> 00:16:49.040
Please give me
those documents, my lady.

00:16:49.750 --> 00:16:53.720
With those, we can indict Vice
Admiral Christopher von Basel.

00:16:54.420 --> 00:16:59.950
For drug trafficking, for leading a secret
criminal organization inside the military...

00:16:59.950 --> 00:17:02.630
...for being the true war criminal
in the defeat at Arlesheim.

00:17:03.880 --> 00:17:07.420
Please give Rear Admiral Keyserling
a chance to clear his name.

00:17:08.450 --> 00:17:14.890
Young man, I cannot cooperate in
making Christopher a criminal.

00:17:14.890 --> 00:17:17.130
I will do what he asked me to.

00:17:18.180 --> 00:17:19.650
Frau Basel...

00:17:19.650 --> 00:17:22.020
I will burn these.

00:17:22.020 --> 00:17:24.700
If you want to stop me,
you must shoot me.

00:17:25.760 --> 00:17:27.440
My lady....

00:17:27.440 --> 00:17:33.010
Rational or irrational, right or wrong,
I'm not concerned about those things.

00:17:33.010 --> 00:17:37.050
If Christopher will not
admit to his own crime...

00:17:37.050 --> 00:17:39.630
...I cannot acknowledge my
husband's crime, either.

00:17:40.450 --> 00:17:43.390
I have no right to.

00:17:43.620 --> 00:17:47.770
I am a petty woman, a
fitting counterpart to him.

00:17:51.510 --> 00:17:52.720
Shoot her.

00:17:52.720 --> 00:17:55.200
I must shoot her.

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:01.600
Go ahead and shoot me.

00:18:06.220 --> 00:18:08.120
No, I can't shoot.

00:18:44.820 --> 00:18:45.840
Michael...

00:19:00.370 --> 00:19:01.310
Johanna...

00:19:03.640 --> 00:19:04.930
Johanna !

00:19:29.220 --> 00:19:33.270
With these documents, we can
indict Vice Admiral Basel.

00:19:33.270 --> 00:19:36.130
You've done such
a favor for us.

00:19:36.130 --> 00:19:38.980
I didn't do anything.

00:19:38.980 --> 00:19:43.390
Lord Keyserling himself
cleared his own name.

00:19:46.160 --> 00:19:47.770
You're right.

00:19:47.770 --> 00:19:53.340
When this incident becomes public, the
official record will be written that way.

00:19:53.340 --> 00:19:56.570
The man who was thought to be
responsible for the infamous debacle...

00:19:56.570 --> 00:20:00.780
...was instead an honorable,
if old-fashioned, knight.

00:20:00.780 --> 00:20:03.840
Such is the way
of "official records."

00:20:04.690 --> 00:20:10.600
The blood that was shed in such events
is to be kept only in the private records...

00:20:10.600 --> 00:20:12.690
...of the ones directly
involved in them.

00:20:15.330 --> 00:20:17.310
Well then, we will see
each other again later.

00:20:20.850 --> 00:20:25.050
The important thing isn't for us
to seek someone's affection...

00:20:25.050 --> 00:20:33.600
...but rather for us to love someone,
and not to regret because of it.

00:20:33.600 --> 00:20:36.880
Just as Michael von Keyserling
did not regret his actions...

00:20:36.880 --> 00:20:40.320
...just as Johanna von Basel
did not regret her actions...

00:20:40.320 --> 00:20:43.900
...neither will
Siegfried Kircheis regret.

00:20:45.460 --> 00:20:49.040
That is his own private
"record" of this incident...

00:20:49.040 --> 00:20:52.250
...as well as proof that he certainly
lived his life in these past few days.

00:21:15.230 --> 00:21:15.980
Lord Reinhard !

00:21:16.650 --> 00:21:17.600
Kircheis !

00:21:19.810 --> 00:21:23.390
We've only been apart for a couple
of days, but how nostalgic it feels.

00:21:25.590 --> 00:21:30.200
At that juncture, if it had been Lord
Reinhard, he would have pulled the trigger.

00:21:30.200 --> 00:21:32.640
Even if he felt hesitant, he would
not have shown such emotion...

00:21:32.640 --> 00:21:36.080
...and would have done
what he had to do.

00:21:36.080 --> 00:21:37.350
Therefore...

00:21:40.670 --> 00:21:43.280
Did you not use your
Executive Class seat ?

00:21:44.250 --> 00:21:47.420
I hate abusing my privileges
when I'm going on vacation.

00:21:47.420 --> 00:21:51.840
Anyway, were you able to enjoy your freedom
in my absence, like a bird with open wings ?

00:21:51.840 --> 00:21:54.190
It's good to be without
a nosy partner, right ?

00:21:54.780 --> 00:22:00.370
No, I can spread my wings only
in the presence of Lord Reinhard.

00:22:00.370 --> 00:22:02.410
That is what I realized.

00:22:05.410 --> 00:22:08.490
Then, I too, will spread
my wings with you.

00:22:08.490 --> 00:22:11.320
First, we should get ourselves a glass
of wine to celebrate our reunion.

00:22:11.320 --> 00:22:14.690
Afterwards, let me hear
what happened, if you like.

00:22:17.820 --> 00:22:25.010
Kircheis has realized he couldn't carry through
with self-conviction the way Reinhard does.

00:22:25.010 --> 00:22:29.900
At the same time, he also understood
the danger of such self-conviction.

00:22:30.900 --> 00:22:37.850
For that reason, they needed each other -
that's what Kircheis came to believe at that time.

